thers, but communication and adaptability issues.\n\nCandidate D: strengths: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), concentrates very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical competence, decision quality), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility). Concerns: regarded as arrogant (crew cooperation, professional communication), relatively weak leadership skills (crew cooperation, maybe decision quality). Also earlier note: \"considered moody\" and \"loner\". So strong problem solving and responsibility, but interpersonal concerns.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best overall fits. The criteria weight: reliability, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility. All are safety-critical.\n\nCandidate B: reliability high, stress high, technical moderate, but attention low (memory for numbers) and cooperation low (nasty remarks). Candidate C: decision quality high, attention high, cooperation moderate (concern for others but communication difficulty), responsibility moderate, technical unknown but likely good. Candidate D: problem solving high, attention high, responsibility high, stress moderate, cooperation low (arrogance, weak leadership). Candidate A: technical high, leadership high, but reliability unknown, cooperation low (unfriendly), stress unknown.\n\nWhich is best? Possibly Candidate C because decision quality and attention are crucial, and concern for others suggests cooperation, despite communication issues. Candidate D's arrogance could be serious for crew cooperation. Candidate B's memory issue could affect safety. Candidate A's unfriendly and health issues may affect reliability.\n\nThus I might keep my vote for Candidate C, but need to address Agent 1's points. I can argue that D's arrogance and weak leadership are more concerning than C's communication issues, and that C's decision quality and attention are critical. Also note that D's \"responds to unexpected events adequately\" is less strong than C's \"makes correct decisions quickly\". Also D's \"concentrates very well\" is similar to C's attention, but D's \"arrogance\" may impair crew cooperation more severely. So I will maintain recommendation for C, but suggest we need to discuss Candidate A as well. Provide evidence.\n\nThus public message: I acknowledge Agent 1's points, but argue that D's interpersonal concerns outweigh his strengths, and C's strengths in decision quality and attention, plus concern for others, make C stronger. I keep vote for C. Also note we still need to discuss A.\n\nProceed."}
